<main id="main">
<section class="phero"><div class="phero-bg" data-parallax="0.15"><img src="/assets/img/photos/jackson-capitol.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/jackson-capitol-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/jackson-capitol.webp 1024w" sizes="100vw" width="1024" height="682" alt="" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"></div><div class="wrap phero-in"><nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><ol><li><a href="/">Home</a></li><li><a href="/counties-and-cities/">Counties &amp; cities</a></li><li aria-current="page">Jackson</li></ol></nav><p class="kicker">Capital Region</p><h1>Jackson Insurance Appraiser for Disputed Property Claims</h1><p class="lede">When your carrier’s number doesn’t match what it will cost to repair your Jackson home or building, the appraisal clause in your policy gives you a way to settle the amount without a lawsuit. We work Jackson-area claims from Belhaven to South Jackson and out into the suburbs.</p><div class="btns"><a class="btn btn-gold" href="tel:+18445371427"><svg class="ico" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 16.9v3a2 2 0 0 1-2.2 2 19.8 19.8 0 0 1-8.6-3.1 19.5 19.5 0 0 1-6-6A19.8 19.8 0 0 1 2.1 4.2 2 2 0 0 1 4.1 2h3a2 2 0 0 1 2 1.7c.1.9.4 1.8.7 2.7a2 2 0 0 1-.5 2.1L8 9.8a16 16 0 0 0 6 6l1.3-1.3a2 2 0 0 1 2.1-.4c.9.3 1.8.6 2.7.7a2 2 0 0 1 1.7 2z"/></svg> Call (844) 537-1427</a><a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/talk-to-an-appraiser/">Free claim review</a></div><ul class="hero-facts"><li><small>County</small><b>Hinds County</b></li><li><small>Region</small><b>Capital Region</b></li><li><small>Inspections</small><b>On site</b></li></ul></div></section><div class="wrap cols"><article class="prose"><div class="glance">
<div><p class="glance-h">Neighborhoods &amp; areas</p><ul class="chips"><li>Belhaven</li><li>Fondren</li><li>Eastover</li><li>North Jackson</li><li>South Jackson</li><li>West Jackson</li></ul></div>
<div><p class="glance-h">Housing mix</p><p>Jackson mixes early-1900s homes in Belhaven and Fondren, large custom homes in Eastover, mid-century brick ranches across North and South Jackson, and newer slab-on-grade subdivisions in the Madison and Rankin County suburbs.</p></div>
<div><p class="glance-h">Storm history</p><ul class="storm-list"><li><b>Feb 2020</b><span>Pearl River flooding in the Jackson metro</span></li><li><b>Feb 2021</b><span>Statewide winter storm and freeze, with widespread burst pipes</span></li><li><b>2022</b><span>Jackson water-system failures, pressure loss and boil-water notices</span></li><li><b>Dec 2022</b><span>Hard freeze and another round of frozen-pipe losses</span></li></ul></div>
<div><p class="glance-h">Local claim risks</p><ul class="chips chips-red"><li>Frozen and burst pipes after hard freezes</li><li>Water losses tied to municipal pressure loss and boil-water events</li><li>Pearl River and creek flooding</li><li>Tree fall on older, shaded lots</li><li>Hail and straight-line wind on roofs</li></ul></div>
</div><h2>Property claims in the capital city</h2>
<p>Jackson is Mississippi’s capital and largest city. It sits mostly in Hinds County, which is unusual in having two county seats, Jackson and Raymond, and the city limits also reach into Madison and Rankin counties. That matters on a claim: your address, your county and sometimes your carrier’s local adjuster pool all shape how a loss gets handled.</p>
<p>We also work claims across the metro, including Brandon, Madison, Ridgeland, Clinton, Pearl and Flowood. Many of those suburbs were built out more recently, so the homes and the disputes look different from the older neighborhoods inside the city.</p>

<h2>What recent Jackson losses have looked like</h2>
<p>Jackson’s claim history over the last several years has been driven as much by water and cold as by wind:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>February 2020:</strong> the Pearl River rose into neighborhoods in northeast Jackson and nearby areas. Flood damage generally falls under a separate flood policy, not your homeowners policy.</li>
<li><strong>February 2021:</strong> the statewide freeze split pipes in attics, crawlspaces and exterior walls.</li>
<li><strong>2022:</strong> the city’s water-system failures brought pressure loss and boil-water notices. Some owners later found plumbing and fixture damage that carriers questioned.</li>
<li><strong>December 2022:</strong> another hard freeze, and another round of frozen-pipe claims.</li>
</ul>
<p>On a water loss, the cause question (sudden pipe failure versus long-term leak, or surface water versus plumbing) is usually a coverage issue. Appraisal decides the amount of loss, not coverage. Once coverage is accepted, though, the scope of drying, tear-out and rebuild is where most Jackson water disputes live. Our <a href="/our-appraisal-services/water-plumbing-loss-appraisal/">water and plumbing loss appraisal</a> page explains how we handle those.</p>

<h2>Belhaven, Fondren, Eastover and older Jackson homes</h2>
<p>Belhaven and Fondren hold many early-twentieth-century homes with plaster walls, original wood floors, tall ceilings and detailed trim. Eastover has large custom homes with high-end finishes. North, South and West Jackson have a lot of brick ranches from the 1960s through the 1980s.</p>
<h3>Where estimates come apart</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>Plaster and trim:</strong> carrier estimates often price drywall patching where the house has plaster and site-built moldings.</li>
<li><strong>Flooring continuity:</strong> water reaches one room of continuous hardwood, and the estimate replaces only that room.</li>
<li><strong>Matching:</strong> older brick, tile and shingles may no longer be made, so a “repair” that can’t match is not a real repair.</li>
<li><strong>Tree fall:</strong> mature oaks and pines shade many of these lots. Many policies cap debris removal per tree and per occurrence.</li>
</ul>

<div class="callout"><b class="callout-t">A note on Yazoo clay</b><p>Much of the Jackson metro sits on Yazoo clay, an expansive soil that swells and shrinks. Foundation movement from soil is usually excluded. Where a covered event, such as a pipe burst or a tree strike, causes the damage, the cost of that damage is a fair subject for appraisal.</p></div>

<h2>How we help Jackson owners</h2>
<p>We start by reading your carrier’s estimate line by line against the actual house: measurements, materials, labor, overhead and profit, and code items. If the gap is real and your policy has an appraisal clause, we can represent you through the demand, the appraiser exchange and, if needed, the umpire. See how that works in our <a href="/appraisal-roadmap/">appraisal roadmap</a>, or start with a <a href="/our-appraisal-services/carrier-estimate-review/">carrier estimate review</a>.</p>
<p>Deadlines in your policy and under state law still apply while you talk to your carrier, so confirm yours with a Mississippi attorney.</p>
<h2>Appraisal services in Jackson</h2>
<p>Every Mississippi Insurance Appraiser service is available in Jackson and the rest of Hinds County, including:</p>
<ul><li><a href="/our-appraisal-services/appraisal-demand-representation/">Appraisal Demand Representation</a></li><li><a href="/our-appraisal-services/home-insurance-appraisal/">Home Insurance Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/our-appraisal-services/commercial-hoa-appraisal/">Commercial &amp; HOA Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/our-appraisal-services/roof-hail-claim-appraisal/">Roof &amp; Hail Claim Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/our-appraisal-services/tornado-wind-damage-appraisal/">Tornado &amp; Wind Damage Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/our-appraisal-services/carrier-estimate-review/">Carrier Estimate Review</a></li></ul>
<h2>Jackson claim questions</h2><div class="faqs"><details><summary>Does appraisal cover damage from Jackson’s water-system problems?</summary><p>Appraisal does not decide whether a loss is covered. If your carrier accepts that a water loss is covered but disagrees on the cost of repairs, appraisal can settle that amount. Whether pressure-related damage is covered depends on your policy wording and the facts.</p></details><details><summary>Do you work claims in Madison and Rankin County suburbs?</summary><p>Yes. We work claims across the Jackson metro, including Brandon, Madison, Ridgeland, Clinton, Pearl and Flowood, and throughout Mississippi.</p></details><details><summary>My foundation cracked. Can appraisal help?</summary><p>Foundation movement from expansive Yazoo clay is usually excluded. If a covered event such as a plumbing leak or tree strike caused the damage and the carrier accepts coverage, appraisal can address the amount of that loss.</p></details></div>
